{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling under docs/kernel.md sections 7 and 7.1: the export of the\nbody judgment, step E1 of the act environment note.\n\nHugh decided the export on 14 November, as statement d7956f05 and\nsection 17 of `notes/2026-11-14-act-environment.md` record it: \"yes\",\non the condition that `judgeAct` gives identical answers on the\nreplay corpus. Section 7.1 of docs/kernel.md holds a head that adds\nto the kernel while a K item is open and closes none. The export\nadds one export to `packages/derive` and closes no K item.\n\nI rule:\n\n1. The export of step E1 does not wait under section 7.1. The\n   owner's decision is the reason. The exception covers one export,\n   the judgment of an intent body under a stated context, split\n   from `actJudged`. It covers nothing else.\n2. The export is kernel under section 7. Promise 9 says that the\n   runtime and the verifier call the same functions. An exploration\n   that runs other code is a second judge, and three partial copies\n   of the judge's admission exist today.\n3. The condition binds the E1 head. `judgeAct` gives the same answer\n   for each entry of the replay corpus before the split and after\n   it. The head shows this with a witness, and its note states the\n   count of entries compared.\n4. The export adds no scope kind, platform name, capability name,\n   field type or reason code. It adds to no K count.\n5. The checker's review 813ce2a5 of the note is the review that\n   section 7 requires. It cites the page and the reason. The E1 head\n   records this ruling in docs/kernel.md section 7, and the review\n   of that head checks the condition of item 3.\n6. Decision A gets its own ruling with its design. The method\n   `explore` on `ScopeApi` stays held, and no step builds it.\n\nThis ruling starts no build. Request E1 follows the landing of the\nnote and Hugh's ratification.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}